# HyperMind implementation workflow

The single source of truth for how to work in this repo is **`spec/`** (kvx).
This file is a GENERATED pointer to it. Do not hand-edit it; edit `spec/workflow.kvx` and run `spec/specgen`.

> spec/hypermind-01/spec.kvx

## Principles

- **Vertical First**: The system is a stack of layers, and it is built as vertical slices through every layer, never one layer at a time. Each wave delivers a runnable end-to-end capability that touches ledger, projections, indexes, cognition, compose, surface, SDK, eval and docs together. A layer without its consumer in the same wave is not done.
- **Task Driven**: Work is driven by spec/hypermind-01/spec.kvx. Pick the next eligible task by dependency wave in your owner lane, do it, mark it, move on.
- **One In Progress**: One task in progress per agent. Non-conflicting tasks in the same eligible wave may run in parallel across lanes; the wave's integration task requires all of them.
- **No False Success**: Never mark a task done that did not meet its acceptance criteria. Surface honest partials. A green test driven by a fake is not done.
- **Read Full**: When tool output is truncated and the rest is retrievable, fetch the full content before reasoning. An information gap is a stop condition.
- **Deliver Complete**: Deliver complete, runnable artifacts. Follow existing repo style. Add no comments or docs beyond what the task asks.
- **Carry Vectors**: When porting from neocortex or cortex-engine, carry the original test vectors and fixtures verbatim. A port that passes new tests but not the old ones is not a port.

## The loop (every session)

1. Read spec/hypermind-01/spec.kvx: [meta] status, [design.*], the [req.*] acceptance criteria, and the [task.*] list with status, wave, owner_lane and requires.
2. Run cg spec ready. Select the lowest-wave pending task in your lane whose every requires is done. Set it in_progress with cg spec start <id>.
3. Read the referenced acceptance criteria and the design sections the task cites. Inspect only current relevant source; PLAN.md and HARNESS-LESSONS.md are rationale, spec.kvx controls.
4. Implement only the declared touches. Publish interface changes in hm-schema and hm-core before dependent lane work consumes them.
5. Run the task verify_cmd for real. Then cg spec done <id>, which runs verify_cmd plus graph checks and records an outcome memory.
6. Commit from the repository root with a natural commit message describing the real change. One task per commit. Never batch tasks and never leave a done task uncommitted.
7. A wave closes only when its integration task is done: the slice journey test passes through MCP, daemon, ledger, restart and recall, and the eval gate for that slice is green in CI.

